    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1011">

                <pb facs="0882" n="766" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg766"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/237.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-28T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1912—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 21, 10 p.m. The President on March 26 authorized by formal order to
                    the Treasury Department exceptions granting permission for the exportation of
                    the shipments, mentioned in your said telegram, to the consignee in Mexico
                    designated by the Mexican Embassy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
